<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saruhan Bey</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1346</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saruhan Bey was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> commander who founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beylik">beylik</a> of Saruhan in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>. In 1313 he took Magnesia, modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manisa">Manisa</a>, from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> and made it his capital in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gediz-river">Hermus</a> valley. He joined the Aydinids in naval raids across the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a> and was at times an ally of Byzantine factions. The province of Manisa was long known by his name.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saruhan-bey.jpg" alt="Saruhan Bey" width="320" height="324" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Uploadalt · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Silver_gigliato_of_Sarukhan_Beg_bin_Alpagi_1313_1348_ruler_of_Lydia_western_Turkey.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
